A schema generated from your DASDL is yours
-------------------------------------------

Stated plainly, because it is the first thing anyone evaluating the generator
asks: the compiler claims nothing over its output. A schema built from your own
database description belongs to you, with no condition attached — the same
position GNU Bison takes on the parsers it generates, and for the same reason.
A tool that claimed a licence over its users' work would be useless as a tool.


